 Fix a standing profile and agent $i$ with dissonance capacity $b_i$.
 \begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
-  \item \emph{Detection.} Suppose the profile is exposed, and let its \emph{detectability} be $D_i>0$: the smallest across expressible theories of the per-period growth rate of $\log E_i^{m}$ (for each theory, the visit rate times the information divergence at its most-detectable inadequate pair; positive because each theory is inadequate at a recurrent pair). Then the expected number of periods until agent $i$'s dissonance is $O(b_i/D_i)$---linear in capacity, inverse in detectability---and at least of order $b_i$.
+  \item \emph{Detection.} Suppose the profile is exposed, and let its \emph{detectability} be $D_i>0$: the smallest across expressible theories of the per-period growth rate of $\log E_i^{m}$ (for each theory, the visit rate times the betting exponent at its most-detectable inadequate pair; positive because each theory is inadequate at a recurrent pair). Then the expected number of periods until agent $i$'s dissonance is $O(b_i/D_i)$---linear in capacity, inverse in detectability---and at least of order $b_i$.
   \item \emph{Robustness.} If instead the profile is not exposed and is entered adequately, agent $i$ spuriously becomes dissonant with probability at most $e^{-b_i}$ (\cref{prop:rest-points}(ii-b)).
